WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:06.580
One of the best relationship books out there
that I think everybody ought to read is The

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:13.539
5 Love Languages by Gary Chapman. I think
it's sold, 3, 4, 5 million copies. It's phenomenal.

00:00:13.539 --> 00:00:20.550
The 5 love languages he talks about are : Quality
Time, Words of Affirmation (saying nice things),

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.560
Gifts, Acts of Service, and Physical Touch.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:31.699
Just like there are 5 love languages in a
relationship, there are 9 love languages that

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:36.090
great entrepreneurs learn on how to speak
with their teammates. I'm going to cover that

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:42.680
here with you today. I hope I explain this
in a way that makes sense to you because,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:48.530
you know everyone is going to maybe need different
things at different times but the entrepreneurs

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:55.190
that eventually build a very big empire learn
these different things on how to deal with

00:00:55.190 --> 00:01:00.940
people. It may not even be all the entrepreneurs;
it's definitely going to be anybody that ends

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:06.189
up leading at a high level. Anyone that leads
an organization at a high level where a lot

00:01:06.189 --> 00:01:09.700
of people are reporting to them, they will
learn -- I don't know if they will master

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:14.799
all 9 of them, but these are 9 love languages
that entrepreneurs speak with their teammates.

00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:17.130
Let me start off with the first one.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.429
#1: We Need You

00:01:21.429 --> 00:01:29.049
Let me explain what this means. In sports,
when a coach goes to a player who isn't performing

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:34.090
and will say, "We can't win a championship.
We need you to come through. We NEED you."

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.770
There are people who need to feel needed.
Sometimes leaders don't do a good job of expressing

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:46.310
the fact that certain people are needed. Certain
people don't care to be needed. To them it's

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.969
like the more they feel needed, the more they
may abuse the relationship. But there are

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:55.819
those that if they feel like they're needed,
the respond in a big way. But it's not everybody.

00:01:55.819 --> 00:01:57.999
Some people if you tell them you need them,
they're kind of like, "Oh, you need me. Without

00:01:57.999 --> 00:02:01.329
me you can't do anything." That's not the
point that we can't do anything without you,

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:05.249
but a great team is about everybody pulling
their own weight, so we need you to step up.

00:02:05.249 --> 00:02:10.959
We need you to improve. The mature leaders
respond to that. And you also learn a lot

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:14.909
about people. One of the languages is learning
how to tell people that you need them. So

00:02:14.909 --> 00:02:19.849
this means you give them responsibility. "I
need you to help me out with this." I say

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:24.409
this over and over again. Steve Kerr, coach
of Golden State Warriors who won a championship

00:02:24.409 --> 00:02:29.989
last year got Andre Iguodala who is an absolute
all star to come off the bench. He said, "I

00:02:29.989 --> 00:02:35.000
need you to come off the bench and play strong
defense. I need you. The team needs you."

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.879
He did that and went into the finals MVP.
Need responsibility, impact.

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:43.060
Impact is very important for people that want
to feel needed.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:47.260
#3: The other language is Recognition.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:55.189
Recognition. Most jobs and most corporate
jobs at least, there is really no recognition.

00:02:55.189 --> 00:03:00.439
If you look at companies that are stagnant,
you will generally see that recognition sucks

00:03:00.439 --> 00:03:05.379
at that company. They don't know how to recognize,
they don't recognize, it's all so much about

00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:09.269
pressure, pressure, pressure. There's no recognition
to make the people feel special about the

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:13.790
efforts they're putting in. Entrepreneurs
that speak this language, you can have a lot

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:19.629
of fun with this. I love recognizing our guys
and sometimes it's just adding your own touch

00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:24.390
to it when you're recognizing. You know, one
time for one of our senior vice-presidents,

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:31.969
Jason -- I got him a 1984 Olympic torch, from
the Olympics. From L.A. And so that's a meaningful

00:03:31.969 --> 00:03:39.629
gift, getting an Ayrton Senna helmet to one
of our buddies, Matt. Getting a signed guitar

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:48.140
by Zeppelin or Guns and Roses. It could be
signed Michael Jordan shoes. It could be a

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:54.099
custom Louis Vuitton bag -- anything. It's
certain things that you recognize. A lot of

00:03:54.099 --> 00:04:06.379
times it may be a plaque. One time we did
9 exotic cars, and you recognize. People need

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:10.609
to be recognized. And there are different
ways you recognize. One is privately

00:04:10.609 --> 00:04:16.280
you recognize them, two, publicly you
recognize them and three, behind their

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:23.650
back you recognize them. Yes, behind people's
back. Let me explain. What is publicly? Publicly

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.530
is in front of everybody, "Hey, great job,
he's the team member of the month, he did

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.060
a phenomenal job, he did this" and you tell
them why they did a great job and you recognize

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:37.370
them. Privately is typically a mature leadership
item that's taking place where, "Listen, I

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:41.220
just want you to know that you've grown a
lot. I certainly hope this doesn't change.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:45.370
But I want to recognize you. I see what you're
doing to improve and the way you've been improving.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:53.009
Thank you." And then nothing is more exciting
than recognition. People run and play sports

00:04:53.009 --> 00:04:56.919
and put their bodies through so many different
things, just to be an all star, just to an

00:04:56.919 --> 00:05:02.380
All American college football player, just
to be an MVP, just to be a champion, because

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.110
recognition means a lot, we need it. Believe
it or not, you need it. Some people may say,

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:09.780
"I don't need any recognition." People who
say they don't need any recognition -- guess

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.280
what they need? They need recognition the
most. They're afraid to put the effort in

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.680
because they may not get it. But recognition
is something that everybody across the board

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:22.220
needs. I don't care how confident a person
is, everybody needs recognition.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:29.830
3, third language -- Praise and Encouragement.
Praise and encouragement is also a thing that

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:34.220
you have to learn. Now keep in mind, non-performers,
you can't recognize them for anything. So

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:38.750
you can't get up there and say, "I want to
recognize this person for not performing."

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.740
So you don't want to take the individuals
that have gone above and beyond and recognize

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.389
everybody else at that level because that
doesn't work. That's not fair. That guy went

00:05:46.389 --> 00:05:51.539
above and beyond everybody else, but you can
definitely praise people and tell them, "Hey,

00:05:51.539 --> 00:05:56.130
good job. I like what you did. You came here
on time today. Good job." You can encourage

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.919
them. You can do this, you can get better.
I expect more than this. It's a language you

00:05:59.919 --> 00:06:05.199
speak. Again, privately, publicly, behind
closed doors. Behind their back is telling

00:06:05.199 --> 00:06:10.280
other people, "I'm seeing his attitude has
changed." That's behind their back. "I'm starting

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:14.849
to see his effort is improving." Then that
gets to them. Behind their back. That's just

00:06:14.849 --> 00:06:17.139
people. It's a language you speak.

00:06:17.139 --> 00:06:19.310
#4: Clear Directions.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:24.259
Clear direction is, if you tell your teammates,
I need you to do this, this, this by then,

00:06:24.259 --> 00:06:26.910
that's a language that you need to speak as
an entrepreneur and a leader, because your

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:31.080
team needs to hear that from you. I need you
to get this done by this date. Can you do

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:36.330
that? This is what I need you to do. I need
this, this, this. That's what I'm expecting.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.940
Okay, no problem, great. Hey, I really want
to move up and. . . No problem. Let me give

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:46.970
you clear direction. You need to do this and
this and this. Great. And by this time. Great.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:51.949
That language, a lot of times people are,
"You can do it. Go get it." Not effective.

00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:58.150
Clear, you need to do this, this, this. Typically
don't overwhelm more than three. Now obviously

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.539
if you're having a leadership retreat and
you're talking for a handful of days and you're

00:07:01.539 --> 00:07:04.629
talking about all these different points,
I get it, but generally if it's one-on-one,

00:07:04.629 --> 00:07:09.729
give them three points in areas that you them
to improve in and give them direction.

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.169
#5:Next 7:07

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:16.069
Most people are not visionaries. So you need
to understand this is not something that naturally,

00:07:16.069 --> 00:07:21.340
there are some people that are visionaries
and then there are those that are not visionaries.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:26.020
But here's the thing that those who are not
visionaries -- sometimes you don't talk about

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:31.050
the vision and the future enough. The great
leaders, the great entrepreneurs, they're

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.919
always selling the future on where we're going
and what things are going to happen. You just

00:07:34.919 --> 00:07:38.669
got to now this. They're constantly selling
the future and what's going to take place.

00:07:38.669 --> 00:07:42.039
What's next. What's exciting about next year.
What's exciting about five years from now.

00:07:42.039 --> 00:07:46.879
Ten years from now, 15, 20 years from now.
By the way, this is what great presidents

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:52.129
do. America's got an incredible future. We're
going to be. . . the greatest days of ours

00:07:52.129 --> 00:07:57.030
are ahead of us, they're not behind us. This
is a vision being cast. We're going to help

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:00.909
the economy, we're going to help America and
the next five, 10, 15, 20 years innovation,

00:08:00.909 --> 00:08:06.229
we're going to land on the moon. John F. Kennedy
-- visionary. We're going to do this. . . visionary.

00:08:06.229 --> 00:08:11.970
Elon Musk, visionary. There's a vision being
sold. Whether you're a visionary or not, if

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.620
you put it as a reminder to constantly work
on explaining the vision and the future and

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.849
where it's going, your team needs to hear
that. Just so you know that. Everybody needs

00:08:18.849 --> 00:08:23.509
to hear what the future looks like in the
company and organization you're part of.

00:08:23.509 --> 00:08:25.409
#6: Dream

00:08:25.409 --> 00:08:30.720
So here's the vision, here's where we're going,
how are my dreams going to become a reality

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:36.010
by this vision? Well when we do this, you're
going to be able to do this, this, this. You're

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:40.430
going to have this life, this money, this
income, this accolades, whatever is important

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:45.329
to the person, but dreams. I was a guy, you
know, every time I'm looking at this picture

00:08:45.329 --> 00:08:51.290
here, this picture never gets old to me, right?
I was a guy that, you know, I was sold a dream.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:54.740
I'm 21 years old (8:51 -- link to this) here
taking a picture with a red Ferrari. Right?

00:08:54.740 --> 00:09:01.510
I was sold a dream. I bought into a dream.
I look at this pictures and I go through and

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:09.140
what excited me was a dream. "Man, one day
if I can do this." Three weeks into Morgan

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:13.450
Stanley Dean Witter, I'm in San Francisco
and 9/11 happened this is me at San Francisco

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:20.120
getting training. I am $49,000 in debt here.
I just passed my series 7, I'm there with

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:24.269
a bunch of other people that are coming from
wealthy families, degrees -- I'm the only

00:09:24.269 --> 00:09:29.800
one in the class without a degree. But I had
a dream. What if? What if this happens? And

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:35.980
I think those that inspire the most to follow
them and work with them, speak the dream language

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:40.640
constantly. So take an inventory. How often
do you speak the dream language?

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:41.899
#7: Involvement

00:09:41.899 --> 00:09:49.350
Let me explain to you what I mean by involvement.
Constantly ask people their opinion. Constantly

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:52.700
ask people for their feedback. Constantly
ask people what they think you need to do

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.029
next. What are your thoughts on this? What
do you think about this? What do you think

00:09:56.029 --> 00:10:01.890
about that? Involvement. People are being
heard. Now if you ask people for their ideas

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:04.959
and you never implement their ideas, then
they're like, "Why do I even give them to

00:10:04.959 --> 00:10:09.329
you. You never do them anyways." But it's
ideas that they give you and then they see

00:10:09.329 --> 00:10:14.160
progress. What if we did this or that? How
can we make the energy better? How can we

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:17.680
make the office better? How can we make the
company better? Everything's coming from that

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:22.139
place, and people are involved to give you
feedback. How can we make our group better?

00:10:22.139 --> 00:10:28.389
How can we become #1? How can we do this?
Involvement.

00:10:28.389 --> 00:10:32.540
#8: Challenging Someone

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:37.910
This sounds strange but great leaders challenge
people all the time. Privately, publicly,

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:43.450
and behind their back. If I have somebody
that I see is making progress, I'm going to

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.870
pull them aside and say, "Listen, I want to
let you know that I see it. You're making

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:50.680
a lot of progress. I'm excited for you. But
I hope you don't slip. I hope you don't slip

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:55.230
again. I hope you get focused. Hey, what's
been your behavior lately? You're acting like

00:10:55.230 --> 00:11:00.200
this whole thing is only around you. Does
the world revolve around you only? Do you

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.139
realize that there's other people that help
you become successful as well? Do you realize

00:11:03.139 --> 00:11:08.389
how much support you had? So that's a challenge
one-on-one. Then publicly may be "Hey, since

00:11:08.389 --> 00:11:11.930
when have we thought we're already there?
Since when are we walking on just because

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:17.019
you guys made $50,000 last month or $100,000
last month or $30,000 last month, since when

00:11:17.019 --> 00:11:22.450
are you financially free already? Since when
are we there already? Why are we behaving

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:28.290
this way? Why are we acting this way? Why
are we doing this? Group. And then, behind

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.480
people's back. I have no problem with, "I
don't know what's been happening. One day

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:38.230
he's in, one day he's out. I hope he improves."
And that gets to them. I'm totally okay with

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:42.910
that. I don't have a problem with that. Phil
Jackson was famous for this, Riley was famous

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:48.089
for this, Belichick is famous for this, Wooden
was famous for this, great coaches are famous

00:11:48.089 --> 00:11:52.550
for this. Great parents are famous for this.
Great leaders are famous for this. Great generals

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:58.329
are famous for this. Why? Because one, it's
showing that nobody is greater than the team.

00:11:58.329 --> 00:12:02.850
Hey, we all need to pull our own red wagon.
We all need to pull our weight. We all need

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:08.540
to put our part together. The show doesn't
revolve around just one player. It doesn't

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:14.389
work out that way. We're a team. Now somebody
typically does more than the rest; you're

00:12:14.389 --> 00:12:18.630
going to get recognized for it, but if not,
if you think you're above everybody and everybody

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.870
is below you and they're not worthy of you
and all this. No, we're not going to do that

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:28.600
either. By the way, most people think, "I
don't want to challenge because people don't

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:32.540
like it." They look at you like they don't
like it. They walk away but when they're in

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:36.990
their car by themselves, this is what they
say, "He's a leader. She's a leader. That's

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:43.170
why I follow him. Can't stand him sometimes.
But that's why he's a leader." And then they

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:47.740
also become leaders who are also willing to
challenge and push other people because they

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:53.310
speak that language behind closed doors. Then
they go through the process that they go through

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:56.910
that people don't liking them and then they
remember how they treated you, then they'll

00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:00.060
call and say, "I just wanted to let you know
that I was a pain in the butt. Thank you so

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:03.839
much. I'm going through it now." Okay, good.
No problem All good. And by the way, don't

00:13:03.839 --> 00:13:06.010
get too comfortable going back to it again,
right?

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:10.190
#9: Listening And then the last language is
actually not a language. The last language

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:16.779
is when you just go "zip" and you simply listen.
Listening. Not easy, because everyone of us

00:13:16.779 --> 00:13:22.880
can improve in all these nine items. Some
of us want to talk more, some want to listen.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:27.070
Listening is a very, very big skill set. Sometimes
it's just sitting there and hearing them out.

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:30.269
Sometimes I have some of my leaders, people
that I'm mentoring that just want to call

00:13:30.269 --> 00:13:35.529
and talk for 40 minutes. I let them. Go ahead.
He knows who he is and she knows who she is.

00:13:35.529 --> 00:13:44.130
I have a call and boom, they just go. No problem.
I'm listening. Listen, listen, listening.

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:48.649
And feedback here, feedback, and I'll take
notes. Feedback, feedback, because I want

00:13:48.649 --> 00:13:53.730
to listen. I don't get on the call and put
them on mute and doing other things. I'm listening

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:57.610
and I'll say, "About that thing you said about
15 minutes ago, what do you think about this?

00:13:57.610 --> 00:14:00.060
I would say this and don't think like this
because I don't think it's healthy for you

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.980
to think this way because it's going to create
more resentment. Okay, great. So listening.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:08.339
Showing interest. Genuinely. All these things
by the way? If it's not genuine, people can

00:14:08.339 --> 00:14:11.639
tell them apart. If it's an act, people can
tell. So it's something that you've got to

00:14:11.639 --> 00:14:16.470
genuinely want to do these things because
you are dealing with people. Anyway,

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:22.949
Paul, give me my pillow. So 9 love languages
of entrepreneurs. This one was fun to put

00:14:22.949 --> 00:14:26.089
together. I was excited about putting this
one together because I know a lot of people

00:14:26.089 --> 00:14:31.680
can work on those nine areas and it will help
with their business. All right, hey, 100,000

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:37.750
subscribers, by August 31 is our goal. We're
making a massive, massive launch of a website,

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:41.930
a domain I just bought for six figures that
will be launching in August. And we need to

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:47.639
get to 100,000 subscribers by August 31. If
you're not subscribed, to this channel, please

00:14:47.639 --> 00:14:51.779
do so. It depends on where you're watching
this video, but subscribe to this channel.

00:14:51.779 --> 00:14:57.209
I think we're at 45,000 subscribers right
now. And invite peers, we're getting a lot

00:14:57.209 --> 00:15:01.519
of people that are campaigning around helping
us to get to 100,000. One guy's saying three

00:15:01.519 --> 00:15:08.790
pages of points on how to get this going,
this should be a million subscribers. By the

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:13.290
way, we don't advertise, we don't do anything,
we have done no advertising. It's purely word

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:17.209
of mouth on how this channel's growing. Some
of our peers and competitors advertise, hundreds

00:15:17.209 --> 00:15:22.149
of thousands of dollars on a monthly basis.
We don't. We have grown it so far organically.

00:15:22.149 --> 00:15:25.699
Now we may do it in the future, but right
now it's organically. And the goal is to get

00:15:25.699 --> 00:15:28.649
this thing to a million and ten million subscribers
eventually in the future where it becomes

00:15:28.649 --> 00:15:33.519
the number one stop for people to go to for
entrepreneurship and we're going to have other

00:15:33.519 --> 00:15:37.819
people that are going to come and do videos
as well for Valuetainment that we'll be recruiting,

00:15:37.819 --> 00:15:42.009
so stay tuned. But first we got to get to
100,000 subscribers on Valuetainment to get

00:15:42.009 --> 00:15:45.279
to that next level. With that being said,
if you watch this video on a completely different

00:15:45.279 --> 00:15:52.389
site, you can always come back to PatrickBetDavid.com
and if you have any questions/comments, please

00:15:52.389 --> 00:15:54.170
comment on the bottom. Take care everybody,
bye bye.

